  "term": "ligand",
  "definition": "A ligand is a molecule that attaches to another molecule, often a smaller one binding specifically to a larger target such as a receptor, antibody, or enzyme. The term can also refer to a molecule that donates or accepts an electron pair to bond with a central metal atom in a coordination complex.",
